{"assets":["/statement-assets/5d7ad331a60d1b0613640bb8efd107723472231237963ff65e8154e6d28af09c.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"930","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Game with String"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Vasya and Kolya play a game with a string, using the following rules. Initially, Kolya creates a string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":", consisting of small English letters, and uniformly at random chooses an integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" from a segment "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[0, len(s) - 1]"},{"kind":"text","text":". He tells Vasya this string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":", and then shifts it "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" letters to the left, i. e. creates a new string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t = sk + 1sk + 2... sns1s2... sk"},{"kind":"text","text":". Vasya does not know the integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" nor the string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":", but he wants to guess the integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":". To do this, he asks Kolya to tell him the first letter of the new string, and then, after he sees it, open one more letter on some position, which Vasya can choose."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Vasya understands, that he can't guarantee that he will win, but he wants to know the probability of winning, if he plays optimally. He wants you to compute this probability. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that Vasya wants to know the value of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" uniquely, it means, that if there are at least two cyclic shifts of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":" that fit the information Vasya knowns, Vasya loses. Of course, at any moment of the game Vasya wants to maximize the probability of his win."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only string contains the string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":" of length "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"l"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(3 ≤ l ≤ 5000)"},{"kind":"text","text":", consisting of small English letters only."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the only number — the answer for the problem. You answer is considered correct, if its absolute or relative error does not exceed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10 - 6"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Formally, let your answer be "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":", and the jury's answer be "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":". Your answer is considered correct if "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/5d7ad331a60d1b0613640bb8efd107723472231237963ff65e8154e6d28af09c.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"technocup\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1.000000000000000\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"tictictactac\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0.333333333333333\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"bbaabaabbb\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0.100000000000000\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example Vasya can always open the second letter after opening the first letter, and the cyclic shift is always determined uniquely."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example if the first opened letter of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" or \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", then Vasya can't guess the shift by opening only one other letter. On the other hand, if the first letter is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" or \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", then he can open the fourth letter and determine the shift uniquely."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"930B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/930/problem/B"}